{"id": "EUVD-2026-103076", "enisaUuid": "6b7344f9-fd3e-389a-9f89-9394885aa7e5", "description": "FastBee through 2.1.0 contains an insecure direct object reference vulnerability that allows authenticated low-privilege users to access other users' device groups because GroupController queries lack owner checks. Attackers, including self-registered users, can supply sequential group IDs to read, overwrite, reassign, rewrite device associations of, or delete other users' groups.", "datePublished": "2026-10-16T17:39:20", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T20:53:32", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:L/VI:L/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@hieuPenguinnn/fastbee-device-group-cross-user-idor", "https://github.com/kerwincui/FastBee/blob/v2.1.0/springboot/fastbee-open-api/src/main/java/com/fastbee/data/controller/GroupController.java#L70-L137", "https://github.com/kerwincui/FastBee/blob/v2.1.0/springboot/fastbee-service/fastbee-iot-service/src/main/java/com/fastbee/iot/service/impl/GroupServiceImpl.java#L37-L143", "https://github.com/kerwincui/FastBee/blob/v2.1.0/springboot/fastbee-service/fastbee-iot-service/src/main/resources/mapper/iot/GroupMapper.xml#L36-L109", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/fastbee-through-2.1.0-idor-via-iot-group-by-id-endpoints"], "aliases": ["GHSA-gm3x-2x46-fc3v", "CVE-2026-111654"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.25, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "c7bdc538-02ec-38bc-a482-3bbdbb06ce7a", "product": {"name": "FastBee", "vendor": {"name": "kerwincui"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.1.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "9e06be48-ba11-30d4-8c57-e835f1bfe237", "vendor": {"name": "kerwincui"}}], "isExploited": false}